#
# `violated_disjunct_first.guard` mirrored: the same two branches, the undecidable one written first.
#
# Same verdict, same exit code, and the same reason -- which is the point of the pair. Whichever order
# the author wrote the branches in, the clause that could not be evaluated is `Enabled !EMPTY`, so
# that is the clause the failure has to name.
#
# This spelling already reported the right reason before the fix, by luck: reading the explanation
# back out of the closed condition record returned the first one recorded anywhere underneath, and
# here the undecidable branch happens to be first. Its mirror image is what showed the attribution was
# positional.
#
rule condition_reason_is_not_positional when Enabled !EMPTY or Port > "abc" {
    Name == "definitely_not_this"
}
